  "scientific_conclusion": [
    "Same-domain donor ranks do not reduce both median and q90 pair error in every domain, and spatial rank permutation does not worsen the median in Swift. Donor-rank dependence is therefore not the common causal repair.",
    "Rolling the query-local likelihood-parameter fields while preserving the ranks worsens the median pair error by factors of 3.68, 2.80, and 1.94 in TNG100, SIMBA, and Swift. The spatial arrangement of predicted parameters is causally important in every domain.",
